From: h96 work order 2026-09-14
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: vdec: fix the VP9 ANC2AXI dirty-mask publication

0027 protects VP9 against the carry-forward reference address that this driver's own comment in
codec_hevc_common.c describes as "kvadraty / vertikal'nye polosy musora" - squares and vertical
stripes of garbage. A CAPTURE slot whose ANC2AXI entry was written while its buffer was not yet
mapped keeps the address of a different buffer; frames decode into it correctly, but every later
frame that uses it as a reference reads the wrong memory. H264 closes this hole in
.program_capture_buf; VP9 had no such path until 0027 added one, driven by the anc_dirty bitmask.

Two defects in how that mask is published.

1. It is a plain u32 read-modify-written from two contexts with no common lock:

     set     codec_vp9_program_capture_buf()  anc_dirty |= BIT(index)
             reached from vdec_vb2_buf_queue(), which holds sess->lock only
     clear   codec_vp9_process_frame()        read it, refresh the table, anc_dirty = 0
             reached from the interrupt thread, which holds vp9->lock

   A set racing a clear loses the bit. Use set_bit() and xchg() so it cannot.

2. In codec_vp9_resume() the reset stood AFTER codec_hevc_setup_buffers(), which is what actually
   rewrites the table. 0027's comment describing the table as "just written" was accurate; an
   earlier draft of this patch claimed the reset ran before the rewrite, and that claim was simply
   wrong about the code. Because .program_capture_buf runs without vp9->lock, a QBUF can set its
   bit while setup_buffers() is mid-rewrite - and that buffer's slot is not in the table being
   written. Clearing afterwards wipes exactly the mark that mattered. The reset now precedes the
   rewrite, which is the ordering the comment always claimed: marks accumulated earlier are
   superseded by the rewrite, and a mark set during or after it survives for the next
   process_frame().

Scope of the consequence, stated accurately: a lost mark does not strand a slot forever. Any later
QBUF on any buffer sets a bit, and codec_hevc_refresh_buffers() rewrites the whole table, so the
stale entry is repaired at the next refresh. The damage is therefore bounded - corruption between
the lost mark and the next refresh - which is consistent with the owner reporting that VP9 seeks
work but the picture breaks up intermittently, and with a systematic defect being ruled out.

This is a race and ordering fix supported by reading the compiled function and its locks. The lost
update has not been observed directly, and that is not claimed.

--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_vp9.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_vp9.c
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
  * Copyright (C) 2015 Amlogic, Inc. All rights reserved.
  */
 
+#include <linux/atomic.h>
+#include <linux/bitops.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-mem2mem.h>
 #include <media/videobuf2-dma-contig.h>
 
@@ -489,8 +491,14 @@
 	 * tablica byla napisana. Vystavlyaetsya v .program_capture_buf (tam
 	 * tol'ko bit, nikakogo MMIO), gasitsya v process_frame - v tot moment,
 	 * kogda proshivka garantirovanno ne dekodiruet.
+	 *
+	 * h96 0028 (13.09.2026): dostup TOL'KO atomarnymi operaciyami. Stavitsya
+	 * iz vdec_vb2_buf_queue() (sess->lock), gasitsya iz treda preryvaniya
+	 * (vp9->lock) - obshchej blokirovki u etih dvuh putej net, poetomu
+	 * obychnyj |= / = 0 teryal by bit, vystavlennyj parallel'nym QBUF, a
+	 * poteryannyj bit = slot navsegda ostaetsya s chuzhim adresom.
 	 */
-	u32 anc_dirty;
+	unsigned long anc_dirty;
 
 	/*
 	 * Nomer pokoleniya formata: +1 na kazhdyj src_change. Nuzhen, chtoby v
@@ -1630,9 +1638,8 @@
 	 * zavershaetsya obnuleniem 32 slotov ANC_CANVAS_DATA, poetomu posle nee
 	 * referensy obyazatel'no propisyvayutsya zanovo, chto nizhe i proishodit.
 	 */
-	if (vp9->anc_dirty) {
+	if (xchg(&vp9->anc_dirty, 0)) {
 		codec_hevc_refresh_buffers(sess, &vp9->common, vp9->is_10bit);
-		vp9->anc_dirty = 0;
 		vp9->stats.anc_refresh++;
 	}
 
@@ -1709,19 +1716,30 @@
 	struct codec_vp9 *vp9 = sess->priv;
 
 	mutex_lock(&vp9->lock);
+
+	/*
+	 * h96 0028: gasim otmetki DO perezapisi tablicy, a ne posle nee.
+	 *
+	 * codec_hevc_setup_buffers() nizhe perepisyvaet tablicu ANC2AXI celikom po
+	 * tekushchemu sostoyaniyu ocheredi, poetomu vse nakoplennye do etogo momenta
+	 * otmetki dejstvitel'no perestayut byt' aktual'nymi. No .program_capture_buf
+	 * vyzyvaetsya iz vdec_vb2_buf_queue() BEZ vp9->lock, tak chto QBUF mozhet
+	 * postavit' bit imenno vo vremya etoj perezapisi - i ego slot v tablicu uzhe
+	 * ne popadet. Esli gasit' POSLE perezapisi (kak bylo), takaya otmetka
+	 * zatiraetsya, i slot ostaetsya s chuzhim adresom, poka ego ne pochinit
+	 * kakoj-nibud' sleduyushchij refresh.
+	 *
+	 * Gasim atomarno: na etom slove rabotaet set_bit(), meshat' ego s obychnoj
+	 * zapis'yu nel'zya.
+	 */
+	xchg(&vp9->anc_dirty, 0);
+
 	if (codec_hevc_setup_buffers(sess, &vp9->common, vp9->is_10bit)) {
 		mutex_unlock(&vp9->lock);
 		amvdec_abort(sess);
 		return;
 	}
 
-	/*
-	 * h96 0027: tablica ANC2AXI tol'ko chto napisana celikom po tekushchemu
-	 * sostoyaniyu ocheredi - nakoplennye otmetki o "podozritel'nyh" slotah
-	 * bol'she ne aktual'ny.
-	 */
-	vp9->anc_dirty = 0;
-
 	codec_vp9_setup_workspace(sess, vp9);
 	codec_hevc_setup_decode_head(sess, vp9->is_10bit);
 	codec_vp9_process_lf(vp9);
@@ -1817,7 +1835,7 @@
 	if (!vp9 || vb->index >= 32)
 		return;
 
-	vp9->anc_dirty |= BIT(vb->index);
+	set_bit(vb->index, &vp9->anc_dirty);
 }
 
